course: dictionary
lesson: 11561
title: Analysis: looking at the parts
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Analysis means studying something carefully by looking at its parts, so that you can understand it. «The scientist made an analysis of the water to find out what was in it.» She did not just look at the water. She tested it, part by part.
explain: You can also make an analysis of a poem. «Our class wrote an analysis of the poem, looking at its rhythm and its word choices.» An analysis is also the report that shows this careful study. When you read a text, ask yourself: what are the parts, and what do they show?
explain: Analysis is a noun, and its plural is analyses. «In the final analysis, the team deserved to win» is a phrase that means when everything has been thought about, the team deserved to win.
fact: Analysis means studying something carefully by looking at its parts.
fact: An analysis is a report or piece of work that explains this careful study.
fact: In science, analysis means testing a substance to find out what is in it.
fact: In maths, analysis of data means looking for patterns, totals and averages.
fact: «In the final analysis» means when everything is considered.
exercise: «The scientist did an analysis of the water to find out what was in it.» In this sentence, what is analysis? | A map of the river | A big wave of water | A party for scientists | *Testing something to find out what is in it
exercise: In maths, what does analysis of data mean? | Drawing pictures of animals | Writing a story about numbers | Counting the seconds on a clock | *Looking for patterns, totals and averages
exercise: «Our class wrote an analysis of the poem.» What is an analysis here? | A poem that is very long | A kind of song for the class | A short holiday in the country | *A careful study of the poem's parts and how they work
test: «In the final analysis, the team deserved to win.» What does in the final analysis mean? | *When everything has been thought about, the team deserved to win | At the end of the game, the team was tired | The referee was very late | The team won the last match of the year
test: What is the plural of analysis? | Analyzes | Analysis | *Analyses | Analysises
exam: What is an analysis? | *A careful study of something's parts, or the report of that study | A game played with a ball | A short holiday in the country | A tool for cutting paper
